1. COVERED MATERIAL AND RIGHTS HOLDER

The Rights Holder is Pavel Chuprunov. Permission requests: chup1runov@gmail.com.
Covered Material means original Sverinav code, documentation, editorial text,
guides and visual assets only to the extent that he holds the relevant
legally enforceable rights. Mere inclusion in this repository establishes
neither originality nor ownership.

This notice claims no exclusive rights in third-party components, official
or open data, public-domain material, unprotectable ideas or facts, a user's
own text, or material owned by another person. Separate licences and notices
continue to govern the material to which they apply.

2. NARROW PERMISSION FOR THE OFFICIAL SERVICE

Residents may access and use https://chup1runov.github.io/Sverinav/ for its
intended end-user functions without a fee to Sverinav. This permission
includes the loading, execution, browser storage and installed-PWA offline
copies technically necessary for that use. It does not authorise a mirror,
independent deployment, software distribution or use of the underlying
editorial or software library in another product.

Users may use the intended copy/share/export functions for their own notes,
prepared submissions and other user output, and retain their own rights in
that output. This does not transfer the underlying code, editorial library,
assets or brand. External services and information retain their own terms.
A replacement official origin requires the Rights Holder's express notice.

3. NO OTHER VOLUNTARY REUSE GRANT

Except for section 2 and rights preserved by section 5, prior express written
permission from the Rights Holder is required for any act requiring his
permission under applicable law. No additional permission is granted to:

- copy, reproduce, publish, distribute, sell, rent, lend, sublicense, transfer
  or otherwise supply Covered Material or its protected parts;
- modify, translate, adapt, package, embed, rebrand or create derivative code,
  documentation, guides, editorial text or visual assets;
- run, deploy, self-host or offer a separate instance, mirror, white-label
  product, software-as-a-service, distributed application or competing
  service using Covered Material;
- integrate protected parts in another product, plugin, service, collection,
  dataset or automated extraction or content-processing pipeline;
- reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble beyond rights preserved in
  section 5;
- remove or falsify applicable authorship, rights, licence or provenance
  notices where doing so requires the Rights Holder's permission;
- use protected Sverinav branding for another product or falsely imply
  affiliation, endorsement or authorisation.

The same reservation applies to commercial, non-commercial, private,
internal, educational, research, charitable, paid and unpaid uses. There is
no general exception merely because a separate copy is free or attributed.
These are reservations of enforceable rights, not an assertion that every
listed act is restricted in every circumstance.

To the extent that applicable law permits a rights reservation for text and
data mining or model training involving Covered Material, those rights are
expressly reserved as well. This does not override a non-excludable statutory
exception, GitHub's contractual permissions, third-party licences or other
rights preserved in section 5. This notice alone is not a technical access
control or a guarantee that a particular opt-out mechanism is legally adequate.

No patent or trademark licence is granted. No registered patent or trademark
is asserted by this notice.

4. EXPRESS, SPECIFIC OWNER APPROVAL

Any additional voluntary permission must expressly identify its recipient,
material or version, permitted acts, purpose, deployment or distribution if
any, duration and other agreed limits, in a written approval from Pavel
Chuprunov. Permission for one recipient, use or version does not extend to
another. No transfer, sublicensing or delegation is authorised unless the
approval expressly provides for it, subject to section 5.

Silence, public availability, a star, a feature discussion, receipt of a
request, a functionality review or payment without an agreement does not
supply that separate approval. GitHub permissions and statutory rights do
not need a separate owner approval under this section. Agreed fees,
termination and other conditions must have their actual contractual basis;
this notice does not invent retroactive terms.

5. PREVAILING PLATFORM, LEGAL AND THIRD-PARTY BOUNDARIES

(a) GitHub. Nothing in this notice withdraws, conditions on owner approval,
charges for, narrows or obstructs rights already granted or required under
the applicable GitHub agreement. This includes public viewing; use,
display, performance and reproduction through GitHub as permitted by that
agreement and GitHub functionality, including authorised forking; and
GitHub's and its affiliates' applicable hosting, processing and other
contractual rights. The applicable agreement determines their actual scope.
This notice neither enlarges nor purports to replace that scope. If any
restriction here conflicts with such a right, the right prevails to the
extent of the conflict. A GitHub-authorised fork is not by itself a new,
unrestricted licence for all uses of its contents. No promise is made that
GitHub offers a per-fork owner-consent control for public repositories.

(b) Law. Nothing removes rights or exceptions that cannot lawfully be
excluded, including applicable lawful-user rights to necessary backup,
observation, study, testing and narrowly permitted interoperability work.
Lawful quotation, criticism, discussion, independent creation and truthful
references are not prohibited. This notice creates no ownership of an idea,
no confidentiality obligation for publicly available code and no restriction
on an act for which no permission is legally required.

(c) Prior and third-party rights. Valid prior grants, specific third-party
licences, official/open-data terms, contributors' rights and other binding
agreements are not cancelled or relicensed by this notice. Their own terms
and applicable law determine their continuation. The Rights Holder's own
acts, and agents acting within his actual authorisation, are not restricted
by a reservation of his rights. No broader permission to others is implied.

6. CONTRIBUTIONS AND PERMISSION PROCESS

Before accepting substantial third-party code, assets or editorial content,
the maintainer and contributor must explicitly settle provenance, ownership
and the permissions needed for incorporation, distribution and any intended
relicensing. A contribution or pull request is not an automatic assignment
of exclusive rights. Applicable GitHub contribution terms remain in place;
a separate contributor agreement may be needed. Non-waivable moral rights
remain unaffected. See CONTRIBUTING.md and LICENSING.md.

7. SUPPORT, PRIVACY AND ENFORCEMENT

A bug report, security report or permission request grants no additional
reuse licence and does not transfer the reporter's rights or private data.
Do not send passwords, identity numbers or private case records in requests.
The notice does not require payment or approval merely to exercise a right
preserved in section 5.

Any restriction, claim, injunction, damages or termination requires an
actual legal or contractual basis. No automatic fine, ownership of another
person's work, or penalty for lawfully viewing or forking is imposed.

8. NO WARRANTY BEYOND MANDATORY OBLIGATIONS

To the extent permitted by applicable law, the service and materials are
provided as available, without a promise of accuracy, uninterrupted access,
fitness, non-infringement or support. No mandatory consumer protection or
liability that cannot lawfully be excluded is excluded.

9. ADOPTION, LATER TERMS AND INTERPRETATION

This version applies prospectively to Covered Material distributed with
this notice from its adoption in the repository's default branch. It does
not rewrite Git history or revoke valid prior grants. Documents expressly
marked as drafts or historical proposals do not grant a different licence.

No automatic conversion to a free/open-source licence is scheduled. Broader
voluntary permissions or a future licensing change require the Rights
Holder's express approval. This notice is a rights reservation and limited
permission, not a claim that merely viewing a page signs a separate contract.
Governing law and forum for any negotiated permission should be settled in
that agreement subject to mandatory law; no blanket consumer forum waiver
is imposed here.

If a restriction is unenforceable, it applies only to the extent lawfully
permitted; the boundaries in section 5 remain fully effective. No provision
is to be read as enlarging the Rights Holder's underlying rights.
